# autotune-am: Auto Tune multimode (issue #205) centering an AM carrier.
#
# The radio is in AM with the 96 kHz spectrum view (the usual wide view; the
# policy requires width <= 100 kHz and a resolution of width/512 <= 250 Hz) and
# the APP 6 "Auto Tune" button is pressed through the user's path.
#
# scenario_settle arms a TEST-ONLY carrier 376 Hz above the dial
# (mocks/mock_dsp.c + mocks/mock_spectrum.h): the AM policy detects a narrow,
# single, dominant carrier, applies ONE bounded correction (the candidate is
# quantized to the 512-bin resolution, 188 Hz at this width: 376 Hz is exactly
# two steps) and verifies it with four NEW frames after the 300 ms guard,
# discarding the first three published spectra. After that it holds the
# destination and opens the 5000 ms Undo window, so the session is still alive
# when the capture happens.
#
# What the fixture *means*: the dial lands on start + 376 and stays there with
# the session live. If the correction were not verified the rollback would return
# the dial to the start, so landing on the correction IS the proof that the
# verify phase passed with fresh frames - not a fixture that kept the first
# write. The real AM carrier at +/-390 Hz and at +/-780 Hz, weak/QRM carriers and
# the CW/CWR precision are the owner's radio (docs/autotune.md).

name autotune-am
screen autotune-am

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 96000

mode am
filter_low 0
filter_high 3000
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
